CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*does not uniquely resolve.*$
--
Verifies that the implicit destructor of a class derived from two
specializations of the same template can be type-checked without
hitting the spurious "symbol '~X' does not uniquely resolve"
diagnostic.  Previously the dereference of the cast `this_expr` to
each base-subobject type had its type overwritten back to the
derived class's type by `typecheck_expr_dereference`, causing
unqualified lookup of `~X` to walk every base's secondary scope and
match more than one destructor whose `base_name` is identical.
